@inject HostInfo Info

@* Below 1024px .sidebar carries a `transform` (it becomes the mobile drawer), and a CSS transform
   makes `position: fixed` descendants resolve against the transformed element instead of the
   viewport. Both popups this component mounts are affected, with different outcomes:

   - Menu's .menu-backdrop is `position: fixed`, so on a phone it only covers this drawer, not the
     whole screen — tapping outside the drawer (but still on the page) will not dismiss this menu.

   - Modal is worse, and is introduced to .sidebar for the first time here (no other component mounts
     one inside the sidebar): Modal.razor.css's `.modal-root` is `position: fixed; inset: 0`, so its
     `inset: 0` resolves against the transformed 300px-wide drawer instead of the viewport, while the
     dialog panel's own width (`min(520px, 100vw - 32px)`) stays viewport-relative — so on a phone the
     About dialog centers on the drawer and hangs off both of its edges, and the scrim dims only the
     drawer, not the page. Worse, tapping to the right of the drawer lands on Sidebar's own
     `.sidebar-scrim` (z-index 49) instead, which closes the drawer — translating the open dialog
     off-screen with it while `_aboutOpen` stays true, so reopening the drawer pops About back up.

   Fixing either properly needs a portal (rendering the backdrop/panel outside the transformed
   ancestor), which is out of scope for this phase. *@
<Menu Placement="MenuPlacement.Top">
    <Trigger>
        <div class="user-card-trigger">
            <span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">@Info.Initials</span>
            <span class="user-text">
                <span class="user-name truncate">@Info.AccountName</span>
                <span class="user-host truncate">@Info.MachineName</span>
            </span>
            <Icon Name="chevron-down" Size="16" />
        </div>
    </Trigger>
    <ChildContent>
        @* No Sign out: the only session concept is the cookie the launch token is exchanged for, and
           there is no user record to sign out of. An item that looked like one would misrepresent the
           security model. *@
        <MenuItem Icon="settings" OnClick="GoToSettings">Settings</MenuItem>
        @* CloseOnClick="false": this row's own action button is just the "Theme" label -- the actual
           control is the ThemeToggle segmented control in Trailing, which is a sibling, not something
           this button triggers. Without this, clicking the label (most of the row, since
           .menu-item-action is flex:1) would dismiss the menu with no theme change and no feedback. *@
        <MenuItem Icon="sun" CloseOnClick="false">
            <ChildContent>Theme</ChildContent>
            <Trailing><ThemeToggle /></Trailing>
        </MenuItem>
        <MenuItem Icon="info" OnClick="ShowAbout">About</MenuItem>
    </ChildContent>
</Menu>

@if (_aboutOpen)
{
    <Modal Title="About SQL Agent" OnClose="() => _aboutOpen = false">
        <dl class="about">
            <dt>Version</dt><dd>@Info.Version</dd>
            <dt>Listening on</dt><dd>@Info.BindUrl (port @Info.Port)</dd>
            <dt>Store</dt><dd class="mono">@Info.StoreDirectory</dd>
            <dt>Account</dt><dd>@Info.AccountName on @Info.MachineName</dd>
        </dl>
    </Modal>
}

@code {
    [Inject] private NavigationManager Nav { get; set; } = default!;

    private bool _aboutOpen;

    private void GoToSettings() => Nav.NavigateTo("/settings");

    private void ShowAbout() => _aboutOpen = true;
}
